   <h3> Service Roles</h3>
   <p>
   
Service roles are jobs that members provide as a service to other members of 
  the guild. These jobs can be a large time commitment for the members providing 
  them. It is asked that you work with the member providing the service and organize 
  a time to meet that is convenient to both. Demanding access to their services 
  &quot;right now&quot; is not tolerated. The services they provide take a lot 
  of time and effort, and should be respected as such.</p>
<p>Note that if the service costs money (i.e. jewelry, alchemy, etc), the service 
  provider will charge at least the cost of materials, or more than cost of materials 
  if their skill is lacking to help with their advancement. The price for the 
  service is up to the member providing the service.</p>
<p><b>Guild Jeweler</b></p>
<p>Responsible for providing jeweler services to Bloodhorde members and outfitting 
  47+ members with needed resist jewelry for dragon raids.</p>
<p><b>Guild Treasurer</b></p>
<p>Responsible for having a &quot;mule&quot; character that will maintain the 
  guild treasury and keep records of donations and withdrawals.</p>
<p><b>Guild Librarian</b></p>
<p>Responsible for having a &quot;mule&quot; character to hold various spell research 
  components (pages, words, runes, etc)

